Attribution

The core idea of a short list of "must-fix" generated-UI patterns (the "seven
cardinal sins") and the soft and polish tells that follow it are adapted and
condensed from the file docs/anti-ai-slop.md of the open-design project
(https://github.com/nexu-io/open-design), which is licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0. That file in turn credits the MIT-licensed refero_skill
(https://github.com/referodesign/refero_skill). The rule list in this repository
is a condensed and reworded adaptation. It was extended with detection logic,
severity levels, configuration, baselines, hooks and evaluation tooling that are
original to this project. The wording of the rules, documentation and linter
messages is original.

Files that contain adapted material
  skills/ui-anti-patterns/references/rules.md
  skills/ui-anti-patterns/SKILL.md
  skills/ui-anti-patterns/scripts/ui-slop-lint.mjs (rule selection)
  Further files are listed under the two works below.

Changes made to the adapted material
  Rewritten in new wording, merged with further rules, and turned into
  machine-checkable rules with tests.

References (read for ideas, no text reproduced)
  "20 signs a website was made by AI", scalr.sg blog
  "How to de-slopify your designs", UX Collective

Further third-party works (version 0.2.0)

This product includes ideas, names and short reworded passages from the two works below. They were read, condensed and mapped onto this skill's own rule ids. No source code from either work is included. The detection logic, fixtures and thresholds of the added rules were written for this project.

1. Impeccable, https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable, version 4.7.0, commit a054369.
   Copyright 2025 Paul Bakaus. Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
   Used in skills/ui-anti-patterns/references/vocabulary.md, skills/ui-anti-patterns/references/rules.md and skills/ui-anti-patterns/scripts/ui-slop-lint.mjs. What was taken is the names and one-line meanings of detector rules (for example side-tab, pulsing-dot, marquee, hard-offset-shadow, radial-halo, grid background, repeating-stripes-gradient, extreme-negative-tracking), and the idea of separating rules for working screens from rules for landing pages, which this skill implements as the operate and persuade profiles. Changes made, reworded, shortened, regrouped and cross-referenced to this skill's rules. Impeccable did not review or endorse this work. The name Impeccable belongs to its author.

